## Purpose

This matrix traces every audited Foundational Survey Fabric Requirement to its downstream:

- Specification section(s);
- Conformance section(s);
- Reference Vector category/categories.

Its governing rule is:

> **Every Requirement must have a downstream home. Every downstream obligation must be traceable back to an authoritative Requirement.**

A missing explicit citation is a documentation-level traceability gap until proven otherwise. It is not automatically an architectural defect.

---

## Traceability Marks

The matrix uses:

```text
E   Explicit
D   Derived
N/A Intentionally outside that downstream framework
```

### Explicit

`E` means the Requirement is explicitly named or included in the cited downstream page's **Requirements Basis**.

### Derived

`D` means the downstream assignment is supported by the Requirement and by the audited architectural scope of the downstream section, but that downstream page's Requirements Basis does not yet explicitly cite it.

### N/A

`N/A` means the Requirement intentionally governs another downstream framework rather than the framework represented by that column.

