```

The substantive Specification content therefore changed materially.

However, during that integration pass the existing **Requirements Basis** ranges at the bottom of each Specification section were preserved.

That distinction matters.

The matrix defines Specification explicitness using those Requirements Basis citations, not merely by whether the body text now contains a rule implementing the Requirement.

Therefore:

```text
Specification section assignment validity
    -> re-reviewed

Specification E/D basis status
    -> unchanged in this pass
```

This is intentional and preserves audit discipline.

A Requirement should not be promoted from `D` to `E` until the downstream Specification page actually cites it in its Requirements Basis.

