## Specification Integration Consequence

The Day #123 Specification integration strengthens the architectural basis for many existing `D` mappings.

Examples include Requirements concerning:

- finite Survey Domain;
- World-space separation;
- exact coordinates;
- precision extension;
- geometry neutrality;
- primitive geometry;
- connectedness;
- transformations;
- deterministic implementation;
- serialization;
- computability.

But stronger substantive support does not itself convert `D` to `E`.

The correct documentation sequence is:

```text
Requirement
    ↓
Specification content implements Requirement
    ↓
Specification Requirements Basis explicitly cites Requirement
    ↓
Matrix mapping may become E
```

